        { q: "Are there cannabis dispensaries in Newport, Maine?", a: "Yes. Newport has three dispensaries: Gram's Five & Dime (95 Moosehead Trail), Karma Cannabis (2 Elm St), and Brothers Cannabis (75 Main St). The town is one of the better-served small communities in interior Penobscot County." },
        { q: "Does Newport Maine have recreational dispensaries?", a: "Yes. Gram's Five & Dime, Karma Cannabis, and Brothers Cannabis all serve 21+ recreational customers. Newport permits adult-use retail and the town's location on the ME-7 / ME-11 corridor makes it a natural stop for central-Maine shoppers." },
        { q: "What is Newport Maine known for?", a: "Newport is a Penobscot County town of ~3,200 residents in central Maine, on the Sebasticook River. It is known for Sebasticook Lake, its role as a service hub for the surrounding rural communities, and its position between Bangor (~25 min NE) and Waterville (~30 min SW)." },
        { q: "What is the closest dispensary to Newport Maine?", a: "Dispensaries in Newport include Gram's Five & Dime, Karma Cannabis, and Brothers Cannabis. For shoppers looking for a wider menu, Bangor is ~25 min NE and Waterville is ~30 min SW on the I-95 corridor." },
      ]}
    />
